<title>USA: CBOT Aug volume falls 2.0 percent from year ago.</title>
<headline>CBOT Aug volume falls 2.0 percent from year ago.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Board of Trade (CBOT) said its futures and options volume totalled 17,446,820 contracts in August, down 2.0 percent from 17,804,387 contracts in August 1995.</p>
<p>The exchange said volume in the first eight months of 1996 had risen 6.4 percent to 153,086,017 contracts from 143,888,960 contracts in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>Volume in major categories and in selected individual contracts is as follows, with volume for August and percentage change followed by August 1995 volume:  </p>
<p>All futures     13,188,058     - 5.5     13,958,866</p>
<p>  Agricultural   3,463,050     - 2.2	3,541,657</p>
<p>  Financial	9,721,913     - 6.6     10,410,334</p>
<p>All options on</p>
<p>	 futures   4,258,762     +10.7	3,845,521</p>
<p>  Agricultural   1,090,472     +23.3	  884,467</p>
<p>  Financial	3,167,986     + 7.0	2,959,921</p>
<p>Futures (individual)</p>
<p>  US T-bonds     6,625,755     - 6.5	7,083,654</p>
<p>  US 10-yr notes 1,865,735     - 8.0	2,028,743</p>
<p>  US 5-yr notes  1,061,750     - 3.5	1,100,490</p>
<p>  Wheat		345,626     -34.5	  527,716</p>
<p>  Corn	     1,144,618     -13.2	1,318,538</p>
<p>  Soybeans	   989,750     +21.2	  816,961</p>
<p>  Soymeal	    490,349     - 0.3	  491,775</p>
<p>  Soyoil	     449,014     +35.9	  330,507</p>
<p>Options</p>
<p>  US T-bonds     2,314,860     +11.9	2,068,987</p>
<p>  US 10-yr notes   603,810     + 7.3	  582,856</p>
<p>  Corn		 455,910     +10.8	  411,329</p>
<p>  Soybeans	   450,494     +55.3	  290,078</p>
<p>-- Chicago Derivatives Desk (312) 408 8750</p>
